From: h0cheung <hcheunh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dsi: stop Elden slave link clocks before their master

Adapt Project-SunUEFI's bonded DSI host shutdown ordering to Elden's
existing command/video bridge path. Keep the clock-source host active
until its peer's link clocks stop. PLL save and final PHY release keep
their positions; other machines and DPU encoder order are unchanged.

Source: Project-SunUEFI be3073644216a413776b973203d4222e8950703a
Link: https://github.com/slwyts/Project-SunUEFI/blob/be3073644216a413776b973203d4222e8950703a/patches/linux/7.2.9/0008-dsi-bonded-stop-slave-first.patch
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_manager.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_manager.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_manager.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_manager.c
@@ -523,16 +523,17 @@
 		    msm_dsi1->phy->cfg->restore_slave_pll)
 			msm_dsi_phy_pll_save_state(msm_dsi1->phy);
 
-		ret = msm_dsi_host_power_off(host);
-		if (ret)
-			pr_err("%s: host %d power off failed,%d\n", __func__, id, ret);
-
+		/* Keep the clock master alive until the slave link clocks stop. */
 		if (is_bonded_dsi && msm_dsi1) {
 			ret = msm_dsi_host_power_off(msm_dsi1->host);
 			if (ret)
 				pr_err("%s: host1 power off failed, %d\n",
 				       __func__, ret);
 		}
+
+		ret = msm_dsi_host_power_off(host);
+		if (ret)
+			pr_err("%s: host %d power off failed,%d\n", __func__, id, ret);
 
 		mutex_unlock(&dsi_bonded_cmd_lock);
 		goto disable_phy;
